🐛 Bug
CPU usage is not increasing by increasing the number of threads when inferring with CPU only libtorch in one process and multiple threads.
To Reproduce
const int THREAD_CNT = 10

torch::jit::script::Module load()
{
    torch::NoGradGuard no_guard;
    torch::jit::script::Module module = torch::jit::load("xxx.jit");
    module.to(torch::kCPU);
    module.eval();
    return module;
}

torch::TensorOptions options = torch::TensorOptions().dtype(torch::kFloat32).requires_grad(false).device(torch::kCPU);

void * working_thread(void * param)
{
    torch::init_num_threads();
    torch::jit::script::Module * module = (torch::jit::script::Module *)param;
    torch::NoGradGuard no_guard;
    while (1) {
        torch::Tensor x = torch::randn(1, 10, options);
        torch::Tensor y = module->forward({x}).toTensor();
    }
    return 0;
}

void main()
{
    // load module
    torch::jit::script::Module module = load();

    // muti-threading
    pthread_t thread_handle[THREAD_CNT];
    for (int thread_idx = 0; thread_idx < THREAD_CNT; ++thread_idx) {
        pthread_create(thread_handle + thread_idx, 0, working_thread, &module);
    }

    // finished
    for (int thread_idx = 0; thread_idx < THREAD_CNT; ++thread_idx) {
        pthread_join(thread_handle[thread_idx], 0);
    }
}

Expected behavior
One process, more threads, higher CPU Usage.
Environment

LibTorch Version : 1.2
OS : Linux
How you installed LibTorch : download from pytorch.org
CPU : 96 cores

Additional context
Here is my experiment result:
I can get 33% CPU usage by 1 process and 1 thread per process.
I can get 66% CPU usage by 1 process and 2 threads per process.
I can get 46% CPU usage by 1 process and 3 threads per process.
I can get 74% CPU usage by 2 processes and 1 thread per process.
I can get 92% CPU usage by 2 processes and 2 threads per process.
I guess there should be a global lock in process range to limit the performance of multi-threading inference.
